description.narrative:
1.1. The SAISE Roadmap for Digital Transformation of the electoral management is implemented;
1.2. Performance, responsiveness, and accuracy of the SAISE during elections ensured;
2.1.1. Electoral education in schools institutionalized;
2.1.2. Civic participation of Moldovan men and women increased;
2.2. Gradual increase of public knowledge on democratic participation achieved through targeted public outreach campaigns;
3.1.1. The performance and transparency of the “Financial Control” module upscaled;
3.1.2. Capacities of political parties on reporting using the “Financial Control” module enhanced;
3.1.3. A network of CSOs monitoring the implementation of the “Financial Control” module in place and functional;
3.2. Roadmap for the scale up of the political parties’ financing and reporting oversight implemented;
4.1. Harmonized electoral legal framework complying with international standards.

comment.narrative:
- SAISE Development Roadmap in place;
- SAISE demonstrated an adequate and stable performance during the 2019 Parliamentary and General Local Elections;
- Joint programs on civic education in place and implemented by the CCET in partnership with the Ministry of Education;
- 75% of Moldovan voters understand the voting procedure;
- 70% of the financial reports are submitted on time;
- 50% of the political parties submit their reports using the “Financial Control” module;
- No Roadmap for the scalling-up of the political parties' financing and reporting oversight available;
- No dedicated CEC human resource for the political parties' financing and reporting oversight available;
- Existing ambiguities in the Electoral Code highlighted in the EOM reports.

1. Audit and Update of the Concept of the State Automated Information System” Elections” and of the Roadmap for Digital Transformation of the electoral management provided;
2.1. Curriculum for the electoral education in schools initiated;
2.2. Participation of Moldovan men and women in electoral education increased through civic education and voter information programs and at least 15,000 direct beneficiaries – reached;
3.1. Technical support for the upgrade of the “Financial Control” module – provided;
3.2. Roadmap for the scale up of the political parties’ financing and reporting oversight – initiated;
4.1. Comprehensive review of the electoral legal framework – initiated based on EOM recommendations and supported by a consultative platform.

